WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.716 --> 00:00:06.018
In a way I think people want it

00:00:06.151 --> 00:00:06.985
to be confusing.

00:00:07.119 --> 00:00:08.353
&gt;&gt; The people behind the scenes?

00:00:08.487 --> 00:00:09.021
&gt;&gt; Yeah.

00:00:09.154 --> 00:00:13.025
&gt;&gt; You got into a tussle

00:00:13.158 --> 00:00:14.426
recently be Bill Maher.

00:00:14.559 --> 00:00:14.926
&gt;&gt; I did.

00:00:15.060 --> 00:00:16.662
&gt;&gt; About critical race theory

00:00:16.795 --> 00:00:17.095
and wokeness.

00:00:17.229 --> 00:00:18.664
When you look at the political

00:00:18.797 --> 00:00:20.365
discourse in our country today

00:00:20.499 --> 00:00:22.267
and the role that media plays in

00:00:22.401 --> 00:00:27.839
it, what do you think?

00:00:27.973 --> 00:00:30.208
It's difficult to try to find

00:00:30.342 --> 00:00:32.411
truly unbiased reporting, news

00:00:32.544 --> 00:00:34.112
that really is straight

00:00:34.246 --> 00:00:34.546
shooters.

00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:36.481
You know, this conversation I

00:00:36.615 --> 00:00:37.883
had with bill, we're talking

00:00:38.016 --> 00:00:39.751
about critical race theory.

00:00:39.751 --> 00:00:42.321
And I think it's imperative that

00:00:42.454 --> 00:00:49.294
it's taught, that we look at our

00:00:49.428 --> 00:00:51.163
history much the same I think

00:00:51.296 --> 00:00:54.066
that Germany has looked at their

00:00:54.199 --> 00:00:58.270
history involve in the wars, one

00:00:58.403 --> 00:01:00.005
and two, and embrace it and say

00:01:00.138 --> 00:01:01.773
this is where we went wrong.

00:01:01.907 --> 00:01:03.208
This is how it went wrong.

00:01:03.342 --> 00:01:05.777
When I see the make America

00:01:05.811 --> 00:01:10.615
great again, my comment is do

00:01:10.749 --> 00:01:14.186
accept that that could possibly

00:01:14.319 --> 00:01:16.355
be construed as a racist remark?

00:01:16.488 --> 00:01:17.889
And most people, a lot of people

00:01:18.023 --> 00:01:20.592
go how could that be racist?

00:01:20.726 --> 00:01:21.793
Make America great again?

00:01:21.893 --> 00:01:24.196
I said so just ask yourself,

00:01:24.329 --> 00:01:26.732
from an African American

00:01:26.865 --> 00:01:28.934
experience, when was it ever

00:01:29.067 --> 00:01:29.801
great in America for the African

00:01:29.801 --> 00:01:32.304
American?

00:01:32.437 --> 00:01:34.773
When was it great?

00:01:34.906 --> 00:01:37.809
So if you're making great again,

00:01:37.843 --> 00:01:39.811
it's not including them.

00:01:39.811 --> 00:01:42.247
&gt;&gt; To end this on a different

00:01:42.381 --> 00:01:46.785
note, for all of the serious

00:01:46.918 --> 00:01:50.088
talk, your co-stars on "Breaking

00:01:50.222 --> 00:01:52.958
bad" say that you are a child

00:01:53.091 --> 00:01:55.494
trapped in a man's body, and

00:01:55.827 --> 00:01:56.728
that they've never known anyone

00:01:56.862 --> 00:01:59.464
who found it so amusing to stuff

00:01:59.831 --> 00:02:01.032
fruit down his pants.

00:02:01.166 --> 00:02:02.334
&gt;&gt; That's -- you know, that kind

00:02:02.467 --> 00:02:11.843
of rumor is what makes me smile.

00:02:11.843 --> 00:02:12.411
&gt;&gt; Rumor or fact?

00:02:12.544 --> 00:02:13.512
&gt;&gt; You know, there can be fact

00:02:13.845 --> 00:02:15.380
to some of these things.

00:02:15.514 --> 00:02:18.550
As someone who comes on a set

00:02:18.683 --> 00:02:20.819
and I lead a cast, whether it's

00:02:20.952 --> 00:02:23.255
on Broadway or the movie or

00:02:23.388 --> 00:02:25.257
whatever, I want to -- I want to

00:02:25.390 --> 00:02:26.691
protect and have fun with my

00:02:26.825 --> 00:02:27.859
cast and crew.

00:02:27.893 --> 00:02:29.861
And sometimes in the 16th hour,

00:02:29.995 --> 00:02:31.863
everybody is dragging, and it's

00:02:31.963 --> 00:02:32.531
like I think we need a little

00:02:32.664 --> 00:02:34.433
perk.

00:02:34.566 --> 00:02:36.401
And so I'll do something silly

00:02:36.535 --> 00:02:39.871
or even borderline stupid in

00:02:39.938 --> 00:02:42.674
order to make everybody wake up

00:02:42.808 --> 00:02:44.242
and laugh and finish the work

00:02:44.376 --> 00:02:45.477
before we all go home.

00:02:45.877 --> 00:02:47.179
&gt;&gt; And what's the stupidest

00:02:47.312 --> 00:02:47.913
piece of fruit you stuffed down

00:02:48.046 --> 00:02:52.451
your pants?

